        "id": 1002926
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-17T20:27:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The parent is containing the C++ collection. The iterator is keeping a reference to the parent until it itself gets GCed. `Persistent` according to the docs just means \"start with a reference count of 1\". The code in the destructor puts back to 0 by calling Unref. There should be no objects kept alive forever.\n\nI updated [my test](https://gist.github.com/greggman/b2ecc05affb560dc88e0c81263112ee6). I checked that I create device in an inner scope(2), create an iterator for `device.features`. destroy the device, and pass out the iterator, and `WeakRef` for the device and the features\n\nIn the middle scope I wait for the WeakRef for the device to say the device and been garbage collected. Then I use the iterator. It works (Before I added the ref it crashed here). I then pass a WeakRef to the iterator out and the WeakRef to the feature.\n\nI then use the WeakRef for the iterator to see it gets collected. It does. And then I watch the WeakRef for the features to see it gets collected. It does.\n\nIt seems to work as expected. The iterator is holding a reference to the features and released when it gets GCed which allows the features to be GCed.",
      "parentUuid": "2462a12c_cb8d6bd8",
